    },
    {
      "source_url": "https://x.com/FBIDirectorKash/status/2009282979923685431",
      "text": "Lawmakers can lie. FBI results don’t. \n\nSince January 2025, @FBISanFrancisco has made 460 plus violent crime arrests and seized drugs equating to over 607,000 lethal fentanyl doses.\n\nGuns seized. Traffickers charged.\n\nFacts over fiction.",
      "author_handle": "FBIDirectorKash",
      "created_at": "2026-01-08T15:16:07Z",
      "has_media": true
    },
    {
      "source_url": "https://x.com/FBIDirectorKash/status/2008928613165408265",
      "text": "Lawmakers can lie. FBI results don’t.\n\nSince January 2025, @NewYorkFBI has made 1,700 plus violent crime arrests and seized over 8 kilograms of fentanyl, preventing more than 600,000 potential deaths.\n125 firearms seized. Major drug networks disrupted.\n\nPublic safety isn’t political, it’s measurable.",
      "author_handle": "FBIDirectorKash",
      "created_at": "2026-01-07T15:48:00Z",
      "has_media": true
    },
    {
      "source_url": "https://x.com/Osint613/status/2012099407341076637",
      "text": "Trump administration reports a 25% drop in national overdose deaths through early 2025, citing reduced fentanyl supply from Mexico and expanded treatment access, according to provisional CDC data.",
      "author_handle": "Osint613",
      "created_at": "2026-01-16T09:47:36Z",
      "has_media": true
    },
    {
      "source_url": "https://x.com/mbruggelivecom1/status/2082479572122001909",
      "text": "Team Trump at DEA have been making real progress on the fentanyl front. A lot of work remains, and partnerships with blue states is needed to make additional gains.\nRead the post from Dr. Emrani, and check the DEA press release from last December.\nhttps://www.dea.gov/press-releases/2025/12/03/dea-launches-fentanyl-free-america-initiative-combat-synthetic-drug",
      "author_handle": "mbruggelivecom1",
      "created_at": "2026-07-29T14:53:15Z",
      "has_media": false
    },
    {
      "source_url": "https://x.com/Patrickwebb/status/2069804700174574040",
      "text": "BREAKING: The DEA allegedly allowed more than 1.8 million fentanyl pills in monitored shipments and deliveries to go unseized between 2023 and 2025, potentially contributing to overdose deaths, per AP.",
      "author_handle": "Patrickwebb",
      "created_at": "2026-06-24T15:27:50Z",
      "has_media": false
    },
    {
      "source_url": "https://x.com/keribla/status/2069384568327536816",
      "text": "This explanation of how they got the story is bonkers https://apnews.com/article/dea-fentanyl-unseized-drugs-new-mexico-reporter-6559cd3579394c8ea7ee30889897375b",
      "author_handle": "keribla",
      "created_at": "2026-06-23T11:38:23Z",
      "has_media": true
    },
    {
      "source_url": "https://x.com/davenewworld_2/status/2069919794682364040",
      "text": "DEA agents in New Mexico let major fentanyl shipments go unseized and allowed the pills to stay in circulation to build cases for years.\n\nA whistleblower says that at least 1.8 million pills went unseized during one investigation.\n\nThat's an insane amount.\n\nThe DEA says its decisions were \"lawful\" and \"consistent\" with Justice Department guidance. \n\nIt's \"lawful\" and \"consistent\" of them to accept risks to vulnerable communities as collateral damage so they can build bigger prosecutions, and then they'll cite the crisis to justify more police funding and more police militarization.",
      "author_handle": "davenewworld_2",
      "created_at": "2026-06-24T23:05:10Z",
      "has_media": true
    }
  ]
